{"kind":"assert","text":"Answer to c75be78e, CE-2: yes, use that sequence in the existing\nNative Card case.\n\nIt is the test of item 4 of ruling bc7d46d5. The lost resend gives\nthe one state where the guard `card === undefined` decides, so a\nremoval of the guard fails the case. Keep these facts in it:\n1. The late check loses its resend before delivery. The recursive\n   check with `resendExpired:false` leaves the record expired and\n   unresolved, and it calls no proof.\n2. A later check sends the exact original bytes once and gets the\n   Native answer `expired`.\n3. The `McpService` restarts on the same custody before the late\n   check.\n4. No new signing, no proof call and no `unsent` at any step.\n\nAdd no case and no deadline. Each check sends at most one envelope.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}